title: Socialisation in the Ruhr
subtitle: The miners strike for the pits.
new-page: true
tags: event
view-if: year = 1919 and month = 2 and crisis = 0
max-visits: 1
on-arrival: {!
RG.startStrike('ruhr', true);
RG.district('ruhr', {militancy: 8});
RG.news('General strike in the Ruhr for the socialisation of the mines', 3);
!}

= Socialisation in the Ruhr

In January a conference of the Ruhr's workers' councils at Essen, Social Democrats, Independents and Communists together, declared the mines socialised and elected a Commission of Nine to run them. Berlin promised to consider it, then sent General von Watter and the Lichtschlag Freikorps to disarm the councils.

Now the councils have called a general strike. In Hamborn and the northern pits our people and the syndicalists lead it. Watter's troops are already shooting.

- @arm: Arm the pits and fight.
- @nine: Stand by the Commission of Nine and the united councils.
- @cells: Use the strike to build the party pit by pit.

@arm
subtitle: [? if lock_uprising = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] The Ruhr will have guns and martyrs. The Freikorps will make it pay.
choose-if: lock_uprising < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids armed action.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_uprising == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.ruhr_line = 1;
Q.lean_offensive += 2;
RG.district('ruhr', {guards: 1, repression: 10, loyalty: 5});
RG.endStrike('ruhr', 'crushed');
!}

In Bottrop and Hamborn armed miners fight the volunteers street by street, and lose.

@nine
subtitle: [? if lock_united_front = 1 : Against the party line: costs Unity. ?] No victory, no massacre, and the Social Democratic miners see us keep our word.
choose-if: lock_united_front < 2
unavailable-subtitle: The [+ leading_faction_adj +] line forbids common work with the social democrats.
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.lock_united_front == 1) { Q.unity -= 10; Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 10; }
Q.ruhr_line = 3;
Q.spd_relation += 4;
Q.uspd_relation += 4;
Q.lean_unionist += 2;
RG.endStrike('ruhr');
!}

@cells
subtitle: Slow work. The cells will still be there the next time the Ruhr rises.
on-arrival: {!
Q.ruhr_line = 4;
Q.e19_ruhr_cells = 1;
Q.lean_luxemburgist += 1;
RG.district('ruhr', {members: 0.1, loyalty: 6});
RG.endStrike('ruhr');
!}

Our organisers go from pit to pit with membership books. When the strike collapses, the new groups stay.
